id: pm-gh1440
title: "GH-1440: validate linked-test context at write time and distinguish execution refusals"
description: "GitHub issue https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1440 reports that a linked command using pm_context_mode=none with the default source workspace is accepted when added and later refused as assertion_failure with exit_code=1 even though the subprocess never ran. Existing none-mode execution isolation from pm-t05d8d remains completed; this new work concerns write-time validation and truthful refusal classification across CLI, SDK and persisted legacy records."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-11T09:41:41.702Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-11T18:12:46.246Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-11T18:08:01.014Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-11T18:08:01.014Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Both add transports and SDK mutations reject none mode without an isolated or snapshot workspace and preserve tracker/history bytes on refusal; legacy invalid records remain non-executable and report a typed config refusal with null exit status; real executed command failures retain assertion_failure and their actual exit codes; public SDK types, contracts, JSON/TOON output, docs and installed Node/Bun behavior agree."
parent: pm-xp1xsw
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "test/create/update reject none context unless workspace mode explicitly selects isolated or snapshot. Readable legacy records refuse execution with config_refusal and null exit; CLI, aggregate and background consumers retain an unsuccessful gate while real exits remain observed."
expected_result: Reject unsafe linked metadata before authoritative writes and never invent subprocess execution evidence.
actual_result: "Canonical sandboxed coverage passes 10,163 tests across 798 files with exact statements 68097/68097, branches 52238/52238, functions 14040/14040 and lines 64757/64757. Typecheck and all static subgates pass after planning-field and typed-edge repairs, including graph/record assurance and mutation controls. Published 2026.10.11 reproduces unsafe context admission and invented exit 1; candidate controls prove unchanged item bytes, no child stdout and null refused exit, while a real child exit 7 remains observed. Item, aggregate and background consumers pass."
