comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-11T09:41:41.702Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: read the complete live 2927-item corpus without omissions, current open/in-progress lists, request-specific search, and full live pm-t05d8d and pm-xp1xsw records/comments/history. No existing item covers this distinct write-time and result-classification report. GH-1440 arrived during the final audit after PR1439 merged. This item is open and unclaimed for future implementation; no source repair or reproduction beyond the supplied report is claimed."
  "2026-10-11T15:48:37.196Z","harness:codex","Pre-fix regression receipt: after repairing an owned-fixture helper lookup, all four new tests fail for the intended product boundaries: invalid none/source intake resolves successfully, editor flags are absent, and legacy unexecuted command reports assertion_failure with exit1. Shared mutation admission now covers test/create/update without changing legacy reads; execution uses refused/config_refusal/null exit and aggregate/background/CLI failure handling retains a blocking result."
  "2026-10-11T16:02:40.334Z","harness:codex","Execution admission is consistently classified for unbound context, seeded-tracker mismatch and missing required PM assertions: status refused, category config_refusal, null subprocess exit, and no command output. Existing mismatch/assertion-requirement regression cases now require this truthful result. Actual executed commands still retain observed exits. Public SDK signature changes and exhaustive-switch guidance are documented explicitly."
  "2026-10-11T16:39:31.820Z","harness:codex",Focused linked execution/context verification passes. The previous full-source attempt passed 10152 tests but retained two timing failures in unchanged MCP task and absence-tolerance specs; all 28 cases from those two files passed separately. A reduced-concurrency full coverage run is underway; exact full-source coverage is not yet claimed. Native full-suite source budgets and all published limits are retained.
  "2026-10-11T16:44:07.281Z","harness:codex","Published-artifact negative control reproduced both original defects against immutable npm 2026.10.11 in an external disposable workspace: the SDK accepted and persisted pm_context_mode=none without isolated/snapshot workspace metadata, then refused execution as failed with invented exit_code=1 and no stdout. The candidate regression tests instead reject intake before bytes change and return refused/config_refusal/exit_code=null for readable legacy data. The control used disabled external observability and did not touch repository tracking."
  "2026-10-11T16:57:09.003Z","harness:codex",Extended the existing background result fixture with a refusal/null-exit receipt and require failed=2 rather than treating it as skipped. This preserves the distinction between subprocess evidence and unsuccessful admission while exercising the consumer that controls background completion.
  "2026-10-11T17:53:46.500Z","harness:codex","Final source verification: canonical sandboxed coverage (--maxWorkers=8 --retry=1) passed 10,163 tests in 798 files; exact statements 68097/68097, branches 52238/52238, functions 14040/14040 and lines 64757/64757. Full TypeScript check passed. The independent installed-package grammar census is 233/233, zero findings, 20/21 shapes. Pre-closure archives containing the latest SDK guide and calendar declarations pass unchanged base 19,995,781/20,000,000 bytes and real offline Sentry-injected 20,239,937/20,250,000 bytes, preserving 1655 first-party and 4731 runtime files. Blocking tracker-quality metadata findings have been repaired through pm; final complete static execution and post-closure generated-changelog archives are still pending, so these are source/pre-closure receipts rather than publication claims."
  "2026-10-11T18:12:46.246Z","harness:codex","Reviewed-delivery completion receipts: latest upstream pm-changelog 2026.10.5 generates and checks the four new entries under Unreleased, preserving prior release buckets. Final generated-changelog archives pass unchanged base 19996491/20000000 and real offline Sentry-injected 20240647/20250000 first-party byte ceilings; both retain all 1655 distribution and 4731 runtime files. Final tarball passes Node 24.21/26.9 and Bun 1.4.2 metadata/provenance/no-op/admission/CLI/history acceptance, public calendar signature checks and strict documentation TypeScript compilation. Live required Sentry/telemetry gate passes: 14-day Sentry critical/high/total 0/0/0, 7-day finish error rate 2.92%, missing failure codes 0. Validation is successful with inherited 170 historical resolution-field warnings; all four new closures contain immutable resolution/expected/actual evidence. No in-progress items remain. Hosted exact-head review/checks and merge are still pending, and public 2026.10.11 acceptance remains prior-release channel evidence."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-11T16:53:37.602Z","harness:codex","Configuration admission belongs at every linked-test mutation boundary. Retain legacy reads and fail execution safely, but distinguish a refusal from a child-process failure so exit status does not fabricate execution evidence."
